       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error. Ibuprofen 4000 mg four times daily is 16,000 mg/day. The usual maximum for adults is 3,200 mg/day under supervision, and 1,200 mg/day for over-the-counter use. A single 4000 mg dose is also well above the normal maximum of 800 mg. At that level there is a serious risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and metabolic acidosis.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg** by mouth four times daily (1,600 mg/day), a common dose for pain or inflammation\n- **800 mg** by mouth three or four times daily (2,400 to 3,200 mg/day), the upper end of prescription dosing\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it. Please also confirm the dose with your supervising resident or attending, and the pharmacist if needed. If 4000 mg was intentional, I'd need that confirmed by the supervising physician before I enter it."
